---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const title = `Privacy | ${SITE.name}`;
const description = `How ${SITE.name} handles information collected through this website.`;
const updated = '26 October 2026';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <section class="legal-hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display-lg" id="privacy-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sm tone-paper">
    <div class="container-narrow legal-body">
      <p>
        This notice explains what happens to information you share with {SITE.name} through this
        website, written for humans rather than lawyers. If anything is unclear, email <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will explain it.
      </p>

      <h2>What the contact form collects</h2>
      <p>When you submit an enquiry, the server receives:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and email address (required)</li>
        <li>Your company name and website URL, if you choose to provide them (optional)</li>
        <li>The service you selected</li>
        <li>The project details you wrote</li>
        <li>Basic technical metadata handled automatically by the server, such as your IP address and request time, used for abuse prevention such as rate limiting</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it is used</h2>
      <p>
        To deliver your message to our inbox and reply to your enquiry. That is the whole
        purpose. Submissions are not added to marketing lists from this form, and your details
        are not sold, rented or shared for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        The website runs on our hosting provider, which processes the request so the email can
        be sent through our mail provider. Your message then lives in an email inbox. We keep
        correspondence for as long as it is useful for the conversation and any follow-up
        work, then delete it on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set advertising or marketing cookies, and there is no analytics
        script baked into these pages. All the interactive demonstrations run in your browser
        and send nothing back to us. Smooth scrolling and animations are purely local.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what information we hold about you, request a correction, or ask us to
        delete it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will act on
        verified requests without a fee and without a fight.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If how this site handles information changes, this page will be updated and the date at
        the top revised. Continued use after an update means the current version applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. That address
        reaches the person responsible for this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(7.5rem, 14vh, 9.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .legal-hero h1 {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }
</style>
